<!--
  SK2023_Atm_datafit_r2_fude_ccqe_full.xml

  The full-131-dial event-engine value/order source of truth for the production
  r2_fude_ccqe systematics arm. Seeded structurally from
  SK2023_Atm_datafit_pfm.xml (repo root, the era-split config); pfm.xml is
  NEVER edited in place.

  Deltas applied vs pfm: 5 sigma fixes (tilt 0.10, nunubar_ratio 0.05, zenith_up
  0.20, zenith_down 0.20, XSecNuTau 0.20); combined neutron_tagging (sigma 0.1)
  swapped for the neutron_tagging_subgev/_multigev split (sigma 0.12 each, from
  SK2023_Atm_datafit_xsec_barr_ntag.xml:322-334); the 4 decay_e_tagging_sk* blocks
  dropped (not in the 131); 26 missing blocks added (2 zenith already had methods,
  24 new). Optional per-nuisance box children (14 dials) = hard truncation
  bounds, verbatim from the engine bounds-build (sk_binned_engine.py:1836-1840);
  absent box child = unbounded (event-engine default).

  ORDER: the 131 <nuisance> blocks are in the flat production order, byte-identical
  to pynu/binned/SK2023_Atm_datafit_r2_fude_ccqe.xml (= the theta-layout of the
  production grid/seed files). All values are from the binned engine
  CANONICAL_DIALS (the physics authority for these dials).

  NOTE: all 131 are emitted under ONE NeutrinoSource block so the
  ParseXML-resolved nuisance order equals the flat production order. Legacy
  tune-block routing (get_flux/get_xsection/get_detector via
  exp.Definition[source]) keys off the PARENT block name, and a 3-block
  segregation (flux under NeutrinoSource, xsec under NeutrinoTarget, detector
  under NeutrinoExperiment) reorders under ParseXML and cannot reproduce the
  flat order (differs at 124/131 positions). PyNuFit therefore routes each dial
  by its per-dial owner lookup (DialOwnerMap, built from the tune classes' own
  method inventories), which makes this flat layout route correctly.
-->
